jobs.description:
Business Analyst IT Systems 
 Amsterdam Schiphol, Noord-Holland 
 As a Business Analyst IT Systems you'll be working at a high tech company and occasionally you will get to travel in the EU and work with great teams that are part of the Communications and Operations departments. Working in a multicultural environment, the English language is important. A BSc. or MSc. education level is required. 
As a premier provider of investor services to asset managers, financial institutions and other institutional investors worldwide - their unique approach to domestic and cross-border solutions, combined with award-winning client service and the expertise of 5,500 professionals in 15 markets, helps their clients achieve their ambitions. This trusted employer, a globally recognised brand are seeking several Business Analysts Systems with preferably an IT background to join the team as a result of internal promotions. 
The Business Analyst IT Systems main responsibility will be to enable change by defining needs and recommending solutions that will deliver increased value for the tech business. 
The Business Analyst will work alongside other members of the project teams and will be involved in all phases of the project lifecycle, but will have primary responsibility for capturing requirements, investigating solutions, supporting the implementation phases of projects, supporting the UAT processes whilst demonstrating the core behaviours that underline the organisation's values. 
 Business Analyst IT Systems key skills: 
-At least a Bachelor's degree, preferable Business or IT related; 
-Minimum of 2 years practical experience as an IT Business Analyst; 
-Experienced with Microsoft Excel; 
-Experienced or strong knowledge of requirements management and/or process modelling; 
-Experienced writing functional requirements and use case specifications; 
-Experienced handling technical documentations; 
-Experienced gathering and defining client's busine...

The office of this employer is easily accessible (free parking) by car and public transport. 
-would like the challenge of working together in an international software team; 
-have a B.Sc. or M.Sc. level education in embedded programming or a comparable education; 
-have at least 5+ years of relevant experience in software development; 
-are an expert in C or C++ programming language; 
-have knowledge of RTOS (real time operating system); 
-experience with microchip embedded controllers and with CAN communication is an advantage; 
-have a working style: solution oriented and pragmatic; 
-Understand and use a technical level of English speaking, Dutch is not a must. 
 Offered to the Senior Embedded Software Engineer; 
As an Embedded Software Professional at this respected company in Amsterdam, you can count on a diverse position in a professional and, in a positive sense, dynamic technical organization. They offer a full-time job and an above-market salary with terms of employment in accordance with the collective labor agreement. Naturally, the gross monthly salary depends on the knowledge and experience presented. In addition, an excellent pension provision is offered. 
 Are you interested in this permanent vacancy at our client? Please forward your CV to john@servicedrivenprofessionals.nl or call +31 (0)6 10 29 91 58. Also, for additional questions you are welcome to get in contact. 
Met vriendelijke groet/ Kind regards, 
M. John Lemmers BSc.
